      "worked": "$\\mathcal{C}_1$ has centre $(1,2)$ and radius $3$; $\\mathcal{C}_2$ has centre $(7,6)$ and radius $2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=\\sqrt{(7-1)^2+(6-2)^2}\\\\d&=\\sqrt{52}\\\\d&=2\\sqrt{13}\\\\r_1+r_2&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $2\\sqrt{13}>5$, the circles are separate and do not intersect.",
